## What the data is

An element is a recurring financial mechanism. A protocol is a SET of elements.
The 29 laws are constraints of the form:
  (subject1 | subject2 | ...) -> term1 + term2 + ...
where each term is a disjunction of elements. The law fires if any subject is
present; it is satisfied if every term has at least one of its alternatives
present. 19 hazard rules name element combinations that are forbidden,
elevated-risk, or unverifiable.

## Your task

Build a Quint specification in /root/DefiElements/formal/ that models this.
Concretely:

1. `atlas.qnt` - the vocabulary: elements, their attributes, the laws as a
   relation, the hazard rules.
2. A state machine where a protocol is ASSEMBLED incrementally: the state is
   the set of elements chosen so far, and an action adds one element.
3. Express as invariants/properties:
   - `closure`: every fired law is satisfied
   - `hazardFree`: no hazard rule has all its elements present
   - whatever temporal property best captures the reflexive loop (question 13)
4. RUN the model checker. `quint verify` or `quint run --invariant=...`.

